<title>HONG KONG: Tricom jumps 75 pct after cash offer.</title>
<headline>Tricom jumps 75 pct after cash offer.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Tricom Holdings Ltd surged HK$0.58 or 75.32 percent to a 52-week high of HK$1.35 in early trade after they resumed trading on Wednesday following a cash offer announcement.</p>
<p>Its shares were steadied at HK$1.18 in late-morning.</p>
<p>Brokers said a big trading discount to the cash offer price boosted investors interest in rushing for the shares.</p>
<p>A subsidiary of China Strategic Holdings Ltd had said in a statement on Wednesday that it had agreed to make a cash offer of HK$1.20 per Tricom share after it bought a 37 percent stake on Tuesday. -- HK newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
</text>
